                <pb facs="0369" n="263" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg263"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blaine to Mr.
                            Egan</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-12-09"><hi rendition="#italic">December 9,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Blaine asks Mr. Egan whether the minister for foreign affairs asked him for
                    the testimony which the Chilean minister insists was requested of him in the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Baltimore</hi> case and was not given.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
